{"name":"Iron River","hex":"#4d504b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"iron","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common, inexpensive metal, silvery grey when untarnished, that rusts, is attracted by magnets, and is used in making steel: a chemical element having atomic number 26 and symbol Fe.","Any material, not a steel, predominantly made of elemental iron."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of the metal iron.","Strong , inflexible."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iron"},{"term":"river","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large and often winding stream which drains a land mass, carrying water down from higher areas to a lower point, oftentimes ending in another body of water, such as an ocean or in an inland sea.","Any large flow of a liquid in a single body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To improve one’s hand to beat another player on the final card in a poker game."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/river"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iron River Township, Michigan","blocks":[{"text":"Iron River Township is a civil township of Iron County in the U.S. state of Michigan. The population was 1,585 at the 2000 census and 1,052 in 2020."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Iron_River_Township%2C_MI.png/330px-Iron_River_Township%2C_MI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_River_Township%2C_Michigan","wikidata":"Q6072825"},{"title":"Iron River, Michigan","blocks":[{"text":"Iron River is a city in the Upper Peninsula of Michigan and the largest city in Iron County. As of the 2020 census, the city's population was 3,007. The city is situated at the southeast corner of Iron River Township, though it is administratively autonomous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Iron_River_MI_Town_Hall.jpg/330px-Iron_River_MI_Town_Hall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_River%2C_Michigan","wikidata":"Q1807922"},{"title":"Iron River (Marquette County, Michigan)","blocks":[{"text":"The Iron River is a 2.7-mile-long (4.3 km) river in Marquette County on the Upper Peninsula of Michigan in the United States. It is a short stream flowing from the outlet of Lake Independence east to Lake Superior."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_River_(Marquette_County%2C_Michigan)","wikidata":"Q16965526"},{"title":"Iron","blocks":[{"text":"Iron is a chemical element; it has symbol Fe and atomic number 26. It is a metal that belongs to the first transition series and group 8 of the periodic table. It is, by mass, the most common element on Earth, forming much of Earth's outer and inner core. It is the fourth most abundant element in the Earth's crust. In its metallic state it was mainly deposited by meteorites."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron","wikidata":"Q677"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Iron_River_%28city%29%2C_MI.png/500px-Iron_River_%28city%29%2C_MI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Iron_River_%28city%29%2C_MI.png/1280px-Iron_River_%28city%29%2C_MI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Iron_River_%28city%29%2C_MI.png/500px-Iron_River_%28city%29%2C_MI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIron_River_(city)%2C_MI.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/I